{"title":"Routh's Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are points on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f07e1a0cd8a769501df7b3695497e535eb3ac44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{AF}{FB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/74833178ce701d5d335fe6c9b66ecb40d0f1bf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\frac{BD}{DC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/515b2bbf19a19445640c6ff02368352cc098d674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{CE}{AE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"62\" height=\"37\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <b>Routh's Theorem</b> states that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa432e9368f5d0d8d3af8c51676097923f806c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[GHI]=\\dfrac{(rst-1)^2}{(rs+r+1)(st+s+1)(tr+t+1)}[ABC]\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239cda04d81c236a617bf26c6c34e361b13d4f18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5); defaultpen(fontsize(10)); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I; A=(10,20); B=(0,0); C=(30,0); D=(20,0); E=(16.66,13.33); F=(5,10); G=(14.585,11.6298); H=(9.998,8); I=(17.5,5); draw(A--B); draw(B--C); draw(C--A); draw(A--D); draw(B--E); draw(C--F); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,NW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,N); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,N); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,I,SW);[/asy]\" width=\"288\" height=\"205\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Routh%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Scale <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />'s area down so that it becomes 1. We can then use Menelaus's Theorem on <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae94ee896a603ce8e44cfa8f816c56a7a9c0540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FHC$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c5d831108ac631d405b8aab9253cc361cb7f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AF}{FB}\\times\\frac{BC}{CD}\\times\\frac{DG}{GA}= 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"177\" height=\"38\" />\nThis means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cde88df2b45dc52b33e2c8b1a2d2975c6f9126e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DG}{GA}= \\frac{BF}{FA}\\times\\frac{DC}{CB} = \\frac{rs}{s+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"213\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Full proof: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Routh%27s_theorem\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Routh%27s_theorem</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Routh%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Menelaus%27_Theorem\" title=\"Menelaus&#39; Theorem\">Menelaus' Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ceva%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Ceva&#39;s Theorem\">Ceva's Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Routh%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018105632\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 145/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5070/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.356      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.356      1 -total\n-